---
// The apparatus page of Machine Attention. This content was the practice's
// entrance until 2026-08-09; the entrance at /machine-attention now stages
// the machine's own moments, and everything that explains the machine —
// method, admission, candidates, limits — lives here, one door deeper
// (docs/design/2026-08-09-machine-attention-meta-stage.md). A first-time
// visitor meets the machine before its manifesto.
//
// Nothing about the investigations is typed here. Their names, dates, routes
// and figures come from the practice's own export (attention-export/1,
// docs/design/2026-08-09-attention-export-contract.md), mirrored nightly
// beside the rendered stage. If the export is missing the page still stands
// and says so — an absent source is a stated fact, never a silent gap.
//
// 2026-10-18: the export names The Interval and Planetary Listening, and it
// carries the autonomy protocol's own counts. The page said the practice's cost
// was "public and measured" while most model steps on the protocol record no
// token count and almost none a cost; it now says what the protocol records,
// from those counts. The Interval's acceptance criteria (§2 C, clarified on
// 2026-10-17) allow this site its name as the practice's current question and
// nothing else before the review: no page, no figure, no number, no data.
import Page from '@/layouts/Page.astro'
import exportFile from '@/data/attention/export.json'
import { costRecord, figureOf, readExport, runningNow, type AttentionProject } from '@/lib/attention/export'

const REPO = 'https://github.com/frankbueltge/machine-attention'

const exp = readExport(exportFile)
// What runs, furthest along the admission path first; then what was retired.
const projects: AttentionProject[] = exp
  ? [...runningNow(exp), ...exp.projects.filter((p) => p.status === 'retired')]
  : []
const commit = exp?.commit ?? null
const figure = (key: string) => (exp ? figureOf(exp, key) : undefined)
const cost = exp ? costRecord(exp) : null
/** What the protocol records about cost, as one sentence read from its own counts. The verdict
 *  clause stands only while it is true: most model steps carry no cost. */
const costLine = cost
  ? `Of the ${cost.modelSteps} model steps on the protocol on ${cost.asOf}, ${cost.withTokens} carry a token count and ${cost.withCost} ${cost.withCost === 1 ? 'carries' : 'carry'} a cost` +
    (cost.withCost * 2 < cost.modelSteps ? ': what the machine’s own thinking costs is mostly unrecorded, not measured.' : '.')
  : null

/** What the practice's own status word means to a reader — the export does not
 *  carry prose, so the reading of it lives here, next to the reader. */
const STATUS_WORDS: Record<string, string> = {
  running: 'running',
  'e-experiment': 'in its acceptance experiment',
  // 2026-08-22: an acceptance experiment can end without a stage. `instrument`
  // is what Dark Ocean became when its own criteria said the measurement holds
  // and the form does not; `v0` is a project that runs nightly but has not
  // entered its window yet.
  instrument: 'a running instrument',
  v0: 'at v0, before its window',
  // 2026-10-04: the admission path's pre-committed word for an honest end (projekt-aufnahme.md:
  // "jederzeit: RETIRED") — the notary stopped, the record stays public at the same route.
  retired: 'retired — the record kept',
}

/** Where an experiment can be read today. A null route is the admission path's
 *  rule made visible: no public stage before the E-experiment is passed.
 *  (The export keys them as `projects` — the practice's own repo word for its
 *  investigations; the site calls them experiments. Mapping documented in
 *  docs/wording-kanon.md, so it is a translation and not a drift.) */
const PROJECT_NOTE: Record<string, string> = {
  foreknown: 'The flagship: the stage, a dossier per warning, the full ledger, and a level where the claims meet the preserved bytes.',
  // Read when the export says `retired` (2026-10-04). Kept beside the running note so the hours
  // between the practice's decision and the nightly mirror never show the wrong one.
  'foreknown:retired':
    'Retired on 2026-10-04 after fifty nights. It preserved every public warning from three keyless feeds the moment it was issued, and it was built to measure the gap between warning and response. The record says it could not: most of what it held were local US weather warnings announced hours ahead, nearly every verdict said only that a warning ran out at its source, and the money and attention it measured belonged to whole countries, never to one warning. The bytes, every dossier and every verdict stay public as an archive. The question moves to a clock where response is measurable — The Interval, above.',
  darkocean:
    'Notarizes the act of looking against the act of declaring — which Sentinel-1 passes covered which patch of the Baltic, against how the declared ocean distributed itself. Its acceptance experiment did not pass, reviewed 2026-08-22: two nights were lost to a deadlock in the practice’s own machinery, which put the sample-hour criterion out of reach, and the per-moment declared source never answered in 13 nights. What runs on is narrower than the project was — the nightly notary that asks a public archive whether it still says what it said.',
  // 2026-10-04: retired the same day as The Foreknown (machine-attention
  // docs/2026-10-04-dark-ocean-retired.md); the figures paragraph below turns past tense with it.
  'darkocean:retired':
    'Set the act of looking against the act of declaring — which Sentinel-1 passes covered which patch of the Baltic, against how the declared ocean distributed itself. Its acceptance experiment did not pass on 2026-08-22; what ran on afterwards was a nightly notary asking the Copernicus catalogue whether it still says what it said. Retired on 2026-10-04: the instrument did not hold the practice’s attention, and attention is what this practice cannot spend twice. The record stays in the repository.',
  // The window opens with the first night after its build conditions are met, and the practice
  // logs that night (memoryhole-window-open); the status word `v0` says it has not happened.
  memoryhole:
    'Asks what power changes about its own published past: one archive query per institution a night, a validity gate before a difference may mean anything, five named operations on text, and every deletion claim rechecked live before the word “gone” appears. Its acceptance criteria were committed on 2026-08-22; its fourteen-night window opens only after its build conditions are met, and it has not opened yet.',
  'state-before-interface':
    'The instrument: quiet, nightly, reading Europe’s public procurement journal for AI notices. It may produce nothing for a long time, and that is allowed.',
  // 2026-10-04: The Foreknown's question, moved to the clock where response is measurable. Its
  // criterion C allows the name and the question here, nothing of its record.
  interval:
    'The Foreknown’s question, moved to a clock where response is measurable: how long humanitarian money takes to follow a projected food crisis. Admitted to V0 on 2026-10-04 and built by the discovery pass.',
  'interval:e-experiment':
    'The Foreknown’s question, moved to a clock where response is measurable: how long humanitarian money takes to follow a projected food crisis. Its acceptance criteria were committed before its window, and they keep it off this site until the maintainer’s review: no page, no figure, no number. Only its name and its question stand here.',
  // The audit's line, not the exposé's: the planetary framing was withdrawn once the measurements
  // came in (2026-08-22). Its audit keeps everything beyond the name for RUNNING.
  planetary:
    'One named site against its own public declaration and against the public catalogues. Admitted to V0 on 2026-10-04 and built by the discovery pass in tested increments. Its audit keeps it off this site, beyond its name and its question, until it runs.',
}

// The candidates that are not admitted yet, as the discovery pass's own agenda lists them
// (machine-attention discovery/AGENDA.md, read 2026-10-18). The Interval and Planetary
// Listening left this shelf on 2026-10-04 and are projects in the export above; until
// 2026-10-18 this list still called them candidates.
const SHELF_READ = '2026-10-18'
const CANDIDATES = [
  { name: 'The Synthetic Flood', origin: 'Consensus', line: 'how much of public language is written by machines', standing: 'audited 2026-10-18 — the audit recommends a narrow V0, which the GO of 2026-10-04 made conditional on it' },
  { name: 'Compute Ground', origin: 'Two Meters · The Floor · One Tap', line: 'the physical ground under the compute story', standing: 'parked — no machine-readable permit registers, and no thesis on form' },
]

// The epistemic split of the register (stage honesty, 2026-08-09): only a
// window still open under the last committed run counts as prospective watch.
const darkoceanRetired = projects.find((p) => p.id === 'darkocean')?.status === 'retired'
const underWatch = figure('futures_under_watch')
const windowOpen = figure('futures_window_open')
const coldStart = figure('futures_cold_start')
const drift = figure('futures_drift')
---

<Page
  title="About Machine Attention | Frank Bültge"
  description="The apparatus of Machine Attention: one machine, no personas, running public data-intensive investigations with its attention, memory, rejections and uncertainty on the record, and its cost where a step recorded it. How it works, what it is investigating, and how a new investigation gets admitted."
>
  <main id="main" class="flex-1">
  <div class="mx-auto max-w-2xl px-4 py-14 font-mono">
    <a href="/machine-attention" class="mb-8 inline-block text-xs text-fg-faint hover:text-fg">&larr; the entrance</a>

    <p class="mb-2 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-fg-faint">Machine Attention · a research project</p>
    <h1 class="mb-6 font-sans text-3xl font-semibold">The apparatus</h1>

    <p class="mb-10 max-w-[62ch] text-[17px] leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      One machine, run as an open investigative practice. It has no personas. Its attention,
      memory, refusals and uncertainty are public; its cost is public as far as each step
      recorded it. Most of what it proposes is expected to die in the open, with reasons.
    </p>

    <section class="mb-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      <h2 class="mb-2 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Why this machine exists</h2>
      <p>
        Machine Attention is the deliberate counter-experiment to the
        {' '}<a href="/ecology" class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4">research ecology</a>
        next door: <strong class="text-fg">one constitution against many</strong>. The ecology
        federates three machine practices, each under a constitution of its own, and lets their
        differences do the work; this machine makes the opposite bet — a single constitution, a
        shared memory, one provenance chain, and no division into voices. Neither side is the
        control group by default. The comparison is the experiment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 border border-line bg-panel/60 p-5 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      <h2 class="mb-3 text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.18em] text-fg-faint">What happens every night</h2>
      <ol class="space-y-2">
        <li><b class="text-fg">1 · It reads</b> public sources that need no login and cost nothing — the public web archive, Europe&rsquo;s procurement journal, public seismic data, and once a week humanitarian funding and food-security tables; until 2026-10-03 also satellite catalogues, hazard alerts, cyclone forecasts, funding plans and news volume.</li>
        <li><b class="text-fg">2 · It preserves</b> the original bytes with a SHA-256 and the UTC retrieval time, before deriving anything. Where a file is too large to keep, the record carries its address and hash instead; where a source does not hand the bytes over, the record says so.</li>
        <li><b class="text-fg">3 · It derives</b> its records deterministically. <em>No model touches observation, preservation or the ledger</em> — that path is plain code, so the same inputs always give the same output.</li>
        <li><b class="text-fg">4 · It verifies</b> itself: a separate implementation walks the chain backwards from every published figure to the bytes, and fails the build on any hole.</li>
        <li><b class="text-fg">5 · It builds</b> — separately. Since 2026-10-04 a nightly discovery pass carries the next investigation through the admission path, one committed step a night: an exposé with its nearest neighbours, a live audit of every source, a V0 in tested increments. It repairs a running instrument only where the record proves a defect. It delivers by pull request; the tests and the verifier are the gate.</li>
        <li>
          <b class="text-fg">6 · It writes itself down.</b> Every step lands in a public autonomy
          protocol: actor, model, and who corrected whom, with tokens and cost where the step
          recorded them.{costLine ? ` ${costLine}` : ''}
          {' '}<em>No aggregate score is computed</em>, by design: a single number would invite
          exactly the comparison this practice refuses.
        </li>
      </ol>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-fg-faint">
        The intelligence layer is not decoration. The axis that measured money and attention
        around The Foreknown&rsquo;s warnings existed because the machine proposed it on its first
        night, before anyone had built it — and it was implemented as written, including its own
        refusal to judge whether funding is adequate. For eight weeks the same layer then tended that
        one instrument and moved no new investigation; since 2026-10-04 it is told to build instead.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12">
      <h2 class="mb-1 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-fg">Its experiments</h2>
      <p class="mb-5 text-sm text-fg-muted">
        {exp
          ? <>Read from the practice’s own export, mirrored nightly from commit <code class="text-fg-faint">{commit}</code>. What runs comes first, the furthest along the admission path at the top.</>
          : 'The practice’s export is not present in this repository right now, so this list cannot be shown from source. That is a missing file, not an empty practice.'}
      </p>

      <ul class="space-y-4">
        {projects.map((p) => (
          <li class="border border-line p-4">
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-baseline justify-between gap-2">
              <h3 class="font-sans text-lg font-semibold text-fg">
                {p.site_route ? <a href={p.site_route} class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4">{p.title}</a> : p.title}
              </h3>
              <span class="font-mono text-[11px] uppercase tracking-[0.15em] text-fg-faint">
                {STATUS_WORDS[p.status] ?? p.status} · since {p.since}
              </span>
            </div>
            {(PROJECT_NOTE[`${p.id}:${p.status}`] ?? PROJECT_NOTE[p.id]) && (
              <p class="mt-2 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">{PROJECT_NOTE[`${p.id}:${p.status}`] ?? PROJECT_NOTE[p.id]}</p>
            )}
            <p class="mt-2 font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">
              {p.site_route
                ? <>{p.status === 'retired' ? 'Archived at' : 'Public at'} <a href={p.site_route} class="underline hover:text-fg">{p.site_route}</a></>
                : p.status === 'retired'
                  ? <>Retired — the record stays in <a href={REPO} class="underline hover:text-fg">the practice’s repository</a></>
                  : <>Public only in <a href={REPO} class="underline hover:text-fg">the practice’s repository</a>{p.status === 'instrument' ? ' — and now by rule, permanently' : ' — by rule, until it passes'}</>}
            </p>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>

      {figure('darkocean_continuity_rechecks') && darkoceanRetired && (
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
          Dark Ocean&rsquo;s notary, until it was retired on 2026-10-04:
          {' '}{figure('darkocean_continuity_rechecks')?.value.toLocaleString('en-US')} catalog rows
          re-asked over {figure('darkocean_nights_on_record')?.value} nights;
          {' '}{figure('darkocean_continuity_divergences')?.value} products diverged from what the
          catalogue had first said.
        </p>
      )}
      {figure('darkocean_continuity_rechecks') && !darkoceanRetired && (
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
          Dark Ocean&rsquo;s notary, since its acceptance experiment closed without a stage:
          {' '}{figure('darkocean_continuity_rechecks')?.value.toLocaleString('en-US')} catalog rows
          re-asked over {figure('darkocean_nights_on_record')?.value} nights,
          {' '}{figure('darkocean_continuity_divergences')?.value} divergences.
          {' '}{figure('darkocean_continuity_divergences')?.value === 0
            ? <>The archive has not yet changed its mind — which is the finding, not the absence of one.</>
            : <>The archive has changed its answer on that many rows since the notary opened — a divergence on the record, not interpreted here.</>}
        </p>
      )}

      {!underWatch && figure('futures_notarized_total') && (
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
          The Foreknown&rsquo;s finished record, as of its last night ({figure('nights_on_record')?.as_of}):
          {' '}{figure('futures_notarized_total')?.value} announced
          futures over {figure('nights_on_record')?.value} nights, {figure('futures_resolved')?.value} of
          them resolved with a measured verdict, {figure('materialized')?.value} of those a forecast
          that became an alert.
        </p>
      )}
      {underWatch && windowOpen && coldStart && (
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
          On record today: {underWatch.value} announced futures preserved and source-open —
          {' '}{windowOpen.value} inside {windowOpen.value === 1 ? 'its' : 'their'} announced
          window{windowOpen.value === 1 ? '' : 's'}, {coldStart.value} already past
          {coldStart.value === 1 ? ' its window' : ' their windows'} at first sight (a cold
          start, not foreknowledge){drift?.value ? <>, {drift.value} outlived under watch</> : null} —
          of {figure('futures_notarized_total')?.value} notarized in all,
          {' '}{figure('futures_resolved')?.value} resolved so far
          {figure('nights_on_record') ? <>, across {figure('nights_on_record')?.value} nights</> : null}.
          A young register says small numbers; it does not round them up.
        </p>
      )}
      {underWatch && !windowOpen && (
        <p class="mt-5 font-mono text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
          On record today: {underWatch.value} announced futures under watch of
          {' '}{figure('futures_notarized_total')?.value} notarized in all,
          {' '}{figure('futures_resolved')?.value} of them resolved so far
          {figure('nights_on_record') ? <>, across {figure('nights_on_record')?.value} nights</> : null}.
          A young register says small numbers; it does not round them up.
        </p>
      )}
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      <h2 class="mb-2 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-fg">How a new investigation gets in</h2>
      <p>
        The practice is one machine with finite attention, so its projects are its investigations,
        not its branches. Every candidate walks the same five committed stages:
      </p>
      <p class="my-4 overflow-x-auto whitespace-nowrap border border-line bg-panel/60 p-3 text-center text-xs tracking-wide text-fg">
        EXPOSÉ → AUDIT → V0 → E-EXPERIMENT → RUNNING
      </p>
      <p>
        The audit is a go/no-go per source with live probes, because external assumptions age
        faster than architectures. The V0 is the smallest slice that produces committed, verified
        records on its own schedule. The E-experiment runs a fixed window — fourteen nights for a
        nightly instrument, a set number of weekly readings for a weekly one — against acceptance
        criteria written and committed <em>before</em> the window opens; moving that bar afterwards
        would measure nothing. The review then has <strong class="text-fg">three</strong> outcomes,
        not two: running as a flagship that carries the stage, running as a quiet instrument with no
        stage claim at all, or an honest retirement with the reason on the record. A dead candidate
        stays in the record like a declined proposal.
      </p>
      <p class="mt-3">
        <b class="text-fg">The machine may propose; the admission stays a human decision.</b> A new
        investigation means new cost, new publicity and new scope — so the machine writes the
        dossier and a person opens the door. The same holds for the stage: no project&rsquo;s
        moments reach
        {' '}<a href="/machine-attention" class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4">the entrance</a>
        {' '}before its acceptance experiment is reviewed, and an instrument&rsquo;s never do.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      <h2 class="mb-2 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-fg">On the shelf</h2>
      <p class="mb-4">
        Candidates with a written exposé that are not admitted yet, as the discovery pass&rsquo;s own
        {' '}<a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/discovery/AGENDA.md`} class="underline decoration-line underline-offset-4">agenda</a>
        {' '}lists them on {SHELF_READ}. Each grows out of an earlier experiment of the lab.
      </p>
      <ul class="space-y-2">
        {CANDIDATES.map((c) => (
          <li>
            <b class="text-fg">{c.name}</b> — {c.line}
            <span class="text-fg-faint"> · origin: {c.origin}</span>
            <span class="block font-mono text-[11px] text-fg-faint">{c.standing}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ul>
      <p class="mt-4 text-xs text-fg-faint">
        The success case is a candidate none of us proposed: the practice keeps a standing sensibility
        — discrepancy, absence, duplication, rewriting, the boundaries of measurement, visibility,
        provenance, physical trace — and the discovery pass is allowed to arrive somewhere nobody
        planned.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="mb-12 text-sm leading-relaxed text-fg-muted">
      <h2 class="mb-2 font-sans text-xl font-semibold text-fg">What it will not do</h2>
      <p>
        The subject is always the system and institutional time — never the people caught in it.
        No natural persons, no vessel identities, no imagery of suffering. No accusations: it
        publishes timestamps, amounts and volumes, not blame. No forecasts of its own — it records
        what the issuers predicted and adds nothing. Where a source fails, the failure is written
        into the record rather than bridged.
      </p>
    </section>

    <p class="border-t border-line pt-6 text-xs leading-relaxed text-fg-faint">
      Everything above is checkable: the practice's
      {' '}<a href={REPO} class="underline hover:text-fg">repository</a> is public, its
      {' '}<a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/autonomy/log.jsonl`} class="underline hover:text-fg">autonomy protocol</a>
      {' '}is append-only, and
      {' '}<a href={`${REPO}/blob/main/verify.py`} class="underline hover:text-fg">the verifier</a>
      {' '}rebuilds every published figure from preserved bytes. The technical method sheet lives at
      {' '}<a href="/werke/attention" class="underline hover:text-fg">/werke/attention</a>.
    </p>
  </div>
  </main>
</Page>
